├── README                          # This file
├── requirements.txt                # Python dependencies
├── data/
│   └── upi_bank_grade_data.csv     # Generated dataset (50K transactions)
└── models/
    └── final_model.pkl             # Trained ML model
```

## 🧠 Model Features

The ML model analyzes the following fraud risk factors:

### High-Risk Indicators
- ⚠️ High-amount transfers (>₹30,000 - ₹100,000)
- 🌙 Late-night transactions (0:00 - 4:00 AM)
- 🏙️ Unusual location changes
- 📱 New device usage
- ❌ Multiple failed attempts (≥3)
- 👤 New receiver/beneficiary
- ⚡ Rapid transaction frequency (6+ in 10 minutes)
- 🤖 Mule/burst fraud patterns
- 🌍 Risky IP regions
- 📞 Recent SIM card change

### Low-Risk Indicators
- 🏪 Merchant payments (safer than peer-to-peer)
- ✅ Verified KYC status
- 🔒 Trusted device
- ⏰ Established account (>30 days old)
- ⏱️ Established UPI app usage (>15 days old)

## 📈 Performance

- **Accuracy**: Optimized for high fraud detection rate
- **Precision/Recall**: Balanced to minimize false positives while catching fraud
- **Real-time Latency**: <100ms prediction time
- **Data Balance**: Handles imbalanced fraud classes realistically

